# App Code — Security Rules

Applies to `app/controllers/`, `app/models/`, `app/libraries/`, `app/helpers/`, `app/core/`.

## Pre-Edit Scan (required)

```bash
# Run on files you will change
rg -n "eval\(|exec\(|shell_exec\(|passthru\(|system\(|unserialize\(|extract\(\s*\$_(GET|POST|REQUEST)" app/
rg -n "\$_(GET|POST|REQUEST|COOKIE)\[.*\].*(\->query|\->where|SELECT |INSERT |UPDATE |DELETE )" app/
```

## SQL Injection

```php
// ❌ NEVER — user input in raw SQL
$this->db->query("SELECT * FROM sma_users WHERE id = " . $_GET['id']);

// ✅ CI Query Builder (preserve existing pattern)
$this->db->where('id', (int) $id);
$this->db->get('users');
```

- Prefer `$this->db->where()`, `insert()`, `update()` with bindings.
- If raw SQL exists — **do not refactor logic**; only add casting/`escape_str` when fixing PHP 8.5 errors in same line.

## XSS

- Views: escape user/DB data — `html_escape()`, `xss_clean()` per existing CI pattern.
- Controllers: do not `echo` `$_POST`/`$_GET` directly into responses.
- JSON APIs: `json_encode` with correct content-type; no HTML in JSON error messages with user input.

## Authentication & Authorization

- Admin actions: verify `$this->ion_auth->logged_in()` + `in_group()` / permissions — **do not remove** during upgrade.
- Session: use CI session + `PHP8SessionWrapper`; no custom session ID from user input.
- Password: do not change `ion_auth` hash method unless PM approves (currently may be sha1 in config).

## Dangerous Functions — Block

| Function | Rule |
|----------|------|
| `eval()` | Never add; report if found |
| `unserialize()` on request data | Never; report |
| `extract($_POST)` | Never add |
| `include`/`require` with user path | Never |

## File Upload

- Keep existing validation (extension, path under `assets/mdata/`).
- Do not widen `allowed_types` or disable checks during upgrade.
- Stored files must not execute as PHP (upload dir should not allow `.php`).

## APIs & Webhooks

- Validate API keys/tokens server-side (`Api.php`, `Webhook.php`, `Restapi5.php`).
- Webhooks: verify signature/source IP if existing pattern does; do not remove checks.

## Fix vs Report

| During PHP 8.5 upgrade | Action |
|------------------------|--------|
| Same-line null fix next to SQL | Add minimal cast/escape only |
| Obvious SQLi/XSS in untouched code | **Report to PM** in summary; fix only if user asks |
| Removed auth check (accidental) | **Revert** — never ship |
